# Voice Pipeline

```
STT (mobile: expo-speech-recognition)
  → resolveVoiceTranscript (voice-pipeline)
      → normalizeSpokenMove
      → resolveMove | resolveDisambiguationVoice fast path
      → resolveNoisyTranscript (chess-core voice/)
  → buildContextualStrings (≤100 iOS strings, spoken phrases prioritized)
  → submitPlayerMove → resolveMove legality gate
```

## Rules

- On-device STT primary (`requiresOnDeviceRecognition` when supported)
- Fuzzy matching lives in `chess-core/src/voice/` — not in typed SAN `resolveMove`
- `normalizeMove` remains pure + table-tested in chess-core
- Disambiguation voice: `resolveDisambiguationVoice` first; tap uses `chooseDisambiguation`
- Auto-submit only when `confidence >= minAutoSubmitConfidence(length)` (90% / 80% / 72% tiers)
- Fuzzy ties on same-destination piece moves return disambiguation candidates for the overlay

## Mobile wiring

`useMatchSpeech` → `resolveVoiceTranscript` → `submitPlayerMove` in `useMatchSession`. See `voice-match` skill.
